---
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<!--
  The page's colophon (奥付, okuzuke): the imprint a Japanese book or
  scroll closes on: who made it, when, how to reach them. Same restraint
  as the hero's signature: a hairline rule, small tracked caps, no card
  grid of social icons. "完" (kanji for "the end") stands in for a mark
  of completion, the way it closes a manga chapter or a scroll.

  Fully static. The old "Haut de page" button (Lenis scrollTo) is now
  a plain anchor to #hero, smoothed by `scroll-behavior: smooth` on
  `html` (see styles/app.css) instead of hydrating a React island for
  one link.
-->
<footer class="border-t border-stone/60 px-8 py-8 sm:px-16 sm:py-10">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <p class="flex items-baseline gap-3 text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-taupe uppercase">
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="font-serif text-sm normal-case">完</span>
      © {year} Tom B.
    </p>

    <nav
      aria-label="Contact"
      class="flex items-center gap-4 text-xs tracking-[0.3em] text-taupe uppercase"
    >
      <a
        href="https://github.com/t-aize"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        class="transition-colors hover:text-clay"
      >
        GitHub
      </a>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-stone">·</span>
      <a
        href="https://linkedin.com/in/tom-bialecki-464a65270"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
        class="transition-colors hover:text-clay"
      >
        LinkedIn
      </a>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-stone">·</span>
      <a href="mailto:tom.bialecki2211@gmail.com" class="transition-colors hover:text-clay">
        Email
      </a>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-stone">·</span>
      <a href="#hero" class="transition-colors hover:text-clay">Haut de page ↑</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</footer>
